# 💬 OIBSIP Level 1 – Task 4: Sentiment Analysis

## 📌 Project Overview

This project focuses on building a **Machine Learning-based Sentiment Analysis system** to classify text data into three sentiment categories: **Positive, Negative, and Neutral**.

The project uses Natural Language Processing (NLP) techniques to preprocess Twitter text, convert the text into numerical features using **TF-IDF**, and train machine learning models to predict sentiment.

Two classification algorithms, **Naive Bayes** and **Logistic Regression**, are trained and evaluated to determine which model performs better.

---

## 🎯 Objective

To build a sentiment classification model that can:

* Identify the sentiment distribution in the dataset
* Preprocess text data using NLP techniques
* Convert text into numerical features using TF-IDF
* Train multiple machine learning classifiers
* Evaluate model performance
* Visualize sentiment distribution
* Generate WordClouds for different sentiment classes
* Analyse incorrectly classified tweets
* Demonstrate a real-world application of sentiment analysis

---

## 📊 Dataset

**Dataset:** Twitter Sentiment Analysis Dataset

The dataset contains Twitter text along with sentiment labels.

### Sentiment Labels

| Category | Sentiment |
| -------: | --------- |
|     `-1` | Negative  |
|      `0` | Neutral   |
|      `1` | Positive  |

### Main Columns

* `clean_text` – Text content of the tweet
* `category` – Sentiment label

The dataset contains a large collection of tweets, providing sufficient data for training and evaluating machine learning models.

